WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.503 --> 00:00:01.877
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.877 --> 00:00:04.238
Today's message is: Be Yourself.

00:00:04.238 --> 00:00:06.799
Over to you, Whoopi Goldberg.

00:00:06.799 --> 00:00:08.982
(explosion noise)

00:00:08.982 --> 00:00:11.846
(rooster crowing)

00:00:11.846 --> 00:00:14.340
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.007
♫ Entspresso keep me going.

00:00:18.856 --> 00:00:22.640
- Well, my life is a
class if I was to say,

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.833
it probably teaches
that you can be yourself

00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:28.500
and an individual if

00:00:30.358 --> 00:00:32.494
you are comfortable with not everybody

00:00:32.494 --> 00:00:34.827
liking you or how you think.

00:00:35.944 --> 00:00:40.111
If you're comfortable with
going against the grain.

00:00:41.473 --> 00:00:44.548
If you're comfortable
with people making fun

00:00:44.548 --> 00:00:47.200
or saying really nasty stuff.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.730
If you're comfortable with all of that,

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.813
then you can be yourself.

00:00:51.696 --> 00:00:52.919
That's the price.

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:55.457
The price of being yourself is, you know,

00:00:55.457 --> 00:00:59.778
other people's angst
about you being yourself.

00:00:59.778 --> 00:01:01.193
- I think this is such
an important message

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:04.113
for entrepreneurs because
if you want to have success,

00:01:04.113 --> 00:01:06.842
as an entrepreneur, in
life, but especially

00:01:06.842 --> 00:01:09.562
as an entrepreneur, if
you want to have success

00:01:09.562 --> 00:01:12.069
it has to come from you being you.

00:01:12.069 --> 00:01:13.667
From you being willing to break the rules.

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.643
From you being willing
to express yourself.

00:01:15.643 --> 00:01:18.706
From you being willing to fail publicly

00:01:18.706 --> 00:01:21.323
and know that even the
fact that you were willing

00:01:21.323 --> 00:01:24.156
to try and fail is an inspiration.

00:01:25.339 --> 00:01:27.475
Use it as an inspiration
not just to yourself,

00:01:27.475 --> 00:01:28.923
but to others around you.

00:01:28.923 --> 00:01:30.499
And the people who are watching you,

00:01:30.499 --> 00:01:32.700
and judging you and
throwing tomatoes at you

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.259
and saying you're not
good enough and saying

00:01:34.259 --> 00:01:37.526
that was such a stupid
mistake and laughing at you.

00:01:37.526 --> 00:01:39.811
(bright music)

00:01:39.811 --> 00:01:41.374
You have to learn to ignore them.

00:01:41.374 --> 00:01:43.654
Because if you just
constantly live your life

00:01:43.654 --> 00:01:45.654
according to other people's judgments

00:01:45.654 --> 00:01:47.248
and expectations of you,

00:01:47.248 --> 00:01:49.169
then you're never going to have success.

00:01:49.169 --> 00:01:50.849
You're living up to somebody's expectation

00:01:50.849 --> 00:01:52.913
who's never done what you want to do!

00:01:52.913 --> 00:01:54.865
Your family or friends or
people in your community

00:01:54.865 --> 00:01:56.961
who are saying that you can't do this,

00:01:56.961 --> 00:01:59.697
and you should be doing this,
you should go down this path

00:01:59.697 --> 00:02:02.065
instead of doing, staying
here and going here,

00:02:02.065 --> 00:02:04.218
you should be going down
this path according to them.

00:02:04.218 --> 00:02:05.850
Well have they done what you want to do?

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.274
So you're living your life according

00:02:07.274 --> 00:02:09.867
to what these people's judgments are?

00:02:09.867 --> 00:02:11.882
You're never going to have success.

00:02:11.882 --> 00:02:14.130
You're just going to be a
smaller version of them,

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:17.011
and chances are, they
haven't done much either.

00:02:17.011 --> 00:02:19.162
So take the little that they've done

00:02:19.162 --> 00:02:22.708
and be smaller because that's not you.

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:25.643
Congratulations, that's a happy life.

00:02:25.643 --> 00:02:28.509
You can't just be a copy of somebody.

00:02:28.509 --> 00:02:31.916
You can't shave your head,
wear a Believe hoodie,

00:02:31.916 --> 00:02:33.627
you come on and do top ten videos

00:02:33.627 --> 00:02:36.339
and expect them to do as well as mine.

00:02:36.339 --> 00:02:38.518
You can't outdo Evan Carmichael.

00:02:38.518 --> 00:02:40.412
You can't out-Evan Evan.

00:02:40.412 --> 00:02:42.476
Just like I can't out-you you.

00:02:42.476 --> 00:02:43.753
Don't copy me.

00:02:43.753 --> 00:02:45.100
Go and do you.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.996
Don't say yes because
somebody wants you to.

00:02:46.996 --> 00:02:48.948
Say yes because it's meant for you.

00:02:48.948 --> 00:02:51.364
The thing that I might
disagree with with Whoopi

00:02:51.364 --> 00:02:54.100
is that to get to the comfort,

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:57.029
you need to go through discomfort.

00:02:57.029 --> 00:02:59.788
It's like saying, don't be afraid.

00:02:59.788 --> 00:03:02.274
It's going to work out, don't be afraid.

00:03:02.274 --> 00:03:04.244
You're going to be afraid!

00:03:04.244 --> 00:03:05.940
It's okay to be afraid!

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.334
It's okay to have fear
standing up to somebody.

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:10.997
It's okay to have fear putting
something out in the public

00:03:10.997 --> 00:03:12.613
that you don't know is
going to work or not.

00:03:12.613 --> 00:03:13.973
It's okay to be afraid.

00:03:13.973 --> 00:03:16.222
It's not don't feel the fear,

00:03:16.222 --> 00:03:19.493
it's feel the fear and do it anyway.

00:03:19.493 --> 00:03:21.763
It's feel that fear that
people are putting on you

00:03:21.763 --> 00:03:24.396
or you're putting on yourself
that this may not work,

00:03:24.396 --> 00:03:26.004
that this expression of myself,

00:03:26.004 --> 00:03:29.580
I'm pouring my heart out here
and people may not accept it.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:30.972
And people may laugh at it.

00:03:30.972 --> 00:03:34.237
People say that it's stupid
and it'll never work.

00:03:34.237 --> 00:03:36.330
Pouring it out there anyway.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:38.413
Because you know that
it has to be released.

00:03:38.413 --> 00:03:39.877
Because you need to know.

00:03:39.877 --> 00:03:41.053
Here's a quick personal example.

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:43.654
When I first started
doing these videos here,

00:03:43.654 --> 00:03:46.765
I did it at Toronto Dance
Salsa and we're in a mall,

00:03:46.765 --> 00:03:48.717
and there's people walking by constantly

00:03:48.717 --> 00:03:51.406
and there's people who
look in every now and then

00:03:51.406 --> 00:03:53.269
and see what's happening in here.

00:03:53.269 --> 00:03:55.399
What's this guy doing in
the dance studio with lights

00:03:55.399 --> 00:03:58.437
and a book behind him talking
and yelling into a camera,

00:03:58.437 --> 00:03:59.800
what's he doing?

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:01.350
And at the start, that was something

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:03.662
that I was sensitive about.

00:04:03.662 --> 00:04:05.761
And in between, it's even worse.

00:04:05.761 --> 00:04:09.428
Like in between the
clips, I have my head...

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:13.391
I have my headphones on, and I'm dancing.

00:04:13.391 --> 00:04:14.224
I'm doing this.

00:04:14.224 --> 00:04:16.182
I'm walking around the studio, doing this.

00:04:16.182 --> 00:04:17.015
You see?

00:04:17.015 --> 00:04:19.566
There's somebody watching me right now.

00:04:19.566 --> 00:04:22.107
That's how I, this is what I'm doing.

00:04:22.107 --> 00:04:23.107
Walking the studio.

00:04:23.107 --> 00:04:24.307
Dancing.

00:04:24.307 --> 00:04:25.812
Thinking about what I'm going to say next.

00:04:25.812 --> 00:04:27.979
And people are walking by.

00:04:29.244 --> 00:04:31.708
And I would let that hold me back.

00:04:31.708 --> 00:04:35.284
I would let their judgments
make me play small,

00:04:35.284 --> 00:04:38.684
so instead of doing my
dancing I'm doing this,

00:04:38.684 --> 00:04:40.508
I'm doing it smaller.

00:04:40.508 --> 00:04:43.060
Why am I letting myself play smaller

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:46.708
because of some stranger's
expectations of me?

00:04:46.708 --> 00:04:49.469
Why are you letting yourself play smaller

00:04:49.469 --> 00:04:52.738
because of strangers' expectations of you?

00:04:52.738 --> 00:04:56.369
You will only have success by being you,

00:04:56.369 --> 00:04:58.331
by letting the thing that is different

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:01.061
about you come through.

00:05:01.061 --> 00:05:03.042
And at the start, since
you're nurturing it,

00:05:03.042 --> 00:05:04.153
since you're starting it off,

00:05:04.153 --> 00:05:06.801
it's the start of anything,
you're going to suck at it.

00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:08.708
It's not going to be the best expression.

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:11.530
It's not going to have a
fantastic result, chances are.

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:12.578
And so don't expect it.

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:14.994
Expect it to fail at
the start, that's okay.

00:05:14.994 --> 00:05:16.602
You keep going.

00:05:16.602 --> 00:05:19.051
If you keep practicing, I promise you,

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:23.189
you'll get to the point
where it's comfortable.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:24.778
Where you don't care.

00:05:24.778 --> 00:05:26.899
Where you can let go
of their expectations.

00:05:26.899 --> 00:05:29.588
Just like working out, your
muscles will get stronger.

00:05:29.588 --> 00:05:31.710
But when you first start doing it,

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:35.548
you need to recognize that
it's going to be scary,

00:05:35.548 --> 00:05:38.211
that it's going to be uncomfortable,

00:05:38.211 --> 00:05:40.776
and it's through that obstacle,

00:05:40.776 --> 00:05:44.373
it's through the discomfort
that you get the comfort.

00:05:44.373 --> 00:05:48.011
Comfort is on the other
side of the discomfort.

00:05:48.011 --> 00:05:50.344
The answer isn't crouch back

00:05:51.508 --> 00:05:54.217
and be a small version of yourself.

00:05:54.217 --> 00:05:55.264
'Cause if you stay here, you're always

00:05:55.264 --> 00:05:57.776
going to stay here, your whole life.

00:05:57.776 --> 00:06:00.588
And you have to break through
to get to what you can be.

00:06:00.588 --> 00:06:02.769
So the question of the
day today is, I'm curious,

00:06:02.769 --> 00:06:05.909
what was the biggest thing
that you had to break through,

00:06:05.909 --> 00:06:07.605
the biggest discomfort that you had

00:06:07.605 --> 00:06:10.272
to break through to be yourself?

00:06:11.245 --> 00:06:12.669
Leave it in the comments below.

00:06:12.669 --> 00:06:14.405
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:06:14.405 --> 00:06:17.080
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Vamsi Polimetla.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.631
Thank you so much for picking up a copy

00:06:18.631 --> 00:06:20.464
of my book, "Your One Word."

00:06:20.464 --> 00:06:22.844
It really, really,
really means a lot to me.

00:06:22.844 --> 00:06:24.599
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:06:24.599 --> 00:06:25.695
I believe in you.

00:06:25.695 --> 00:06:27.804
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:06:27.804 --> 00:06:29.924
and whatever your one word is.

00:06:29.924 --> 00:06:32.348
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:06:32.348 --> 00:06:34.789
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:06:34.789 --> 00:06:37.069
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:06:37.069 --> 00:06:40.736
♫ Entspresso keep me going.

